$\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{CMg}$ Br can be prepared by the reaction of $\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\mathrm{C}=\mathrm{CH}$ with $\mathrm{CH}_{3} \mathrm{MgBr}$. This
method is used in preparation of higher alkynes from lower alkynes. The chemical equation for the formation of $\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{CMgBr}$ is given below

\begin{array}{r}
\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{CH}+\mathrm{CH}_{3} \mathrm{MgBr} \longrightarrow \\
\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{CMg} X
\end{array}

